# rule.forbid.unit.remote-boundaries

## .what
unit tests (`.test.ts`) must not cross remote boundaries. touches fs, db, or network → it is an integration test (`.integration.test.ts`)

## .why
unit = atomic logic, fast, deterministic, parallel. remote boundaries add flake + latency. mocks hide the boundary and lie

## .remote boundaries
- filesystem: fs.readFile/writeFile, real paths
- database: queries, dao calls
- network: fetch, http clients, sdk calls

## .instead of mocks
- fakes injected via context (dependency injection): `sendInvoice({ invoice }, { svcEmail: { send: async () => ({ success: true }) } })`
- real dependency → move to `.integration.test.ts`

## .classification
- pure logic, no i/o, injected deps → unit `.test.ts`
- touches db, fs, network → integration `.integration.test.ts`
- blackbox via built contract → acceptance `.acceptance.test.ts`

## .enforcement
- unit test that crosses a remote boundary = blocker
- mock usage in unit tests = blocker

## .see also
rule.forbid.integration.mocks · rule.forbid.acceptance.mocks · rule.require.test-coverage-by-grain
